1
00:00:00,382 --> 00:00:01,629
Last video ended here.

2
00:00:02,232 --> 00:00:04,456
Forty metres of fencing make three sides of

3
00:00:04,476 --> 00:00:06,641
a sheep pen, and an old stone wall

4
00:00:06,721 --> 00:00:07,342
makes the fourth.

5
00:00:08,325 --> 00:00:09,107
Seen from above,

6
00:00:09,651 --> 00:00:10,454
let's try some shapes.

7
00:00:11,297 --> 00:00:13,481
Five metres out from the wall leaves thirty

8
00:00:13,522 --> 00:00:15,485
metres along it, so the area is a

9
00:00:15,546 --> 00:00:16,688
hundred and fifty square metres.

10
00:00:17,554 --> 00:00:19,403
Fifteen out leaves ten along,

11
00:00:19,948 --> 00:00:20,832
a hundred and fifty again.

12
00:00:21,835 --> 00:00:24,120
A square pen, thirteen and a third metres

13
00:00:24,181 --> 00:00:26,285
each way, gives about a hundred and seventy-eight.

14
00:00:26,969 --> 00:00:29,722
But ten out and twenty along gives two

15
00:00:29,804 --> 00:00:30,125
hundred.

16
00:00:30,669 --> 00:00:32,324
So the square isn't the best shape here.

17
00:00:33,029 --> 00:00:34,313
How do we find the best one, and

18
00:00:34,354 --> 00:00:35,437
be sure nothing beats it?

19
00:00:36,301 --> 00:00:38,130
Start by naming what can change.

20
00:00:38,612 --> 00:00:40,901
Let x metres be each side out from

21
00:00:40,942 --> 00:00:43,432
the wall, and y metres the side along

22
00:00:43,473 --> 00:00:43,532
it.

23
00:00:44,096 --> 00:00:46,645
The fence covers x, y and x, so

24
00:00:47,027 --> 00:00:49,235
two x plus y equals forty.

25
00:00:49,717 --> 00:00:52,144
That's the constraint, a fixed total that links

26
00:00:52,165 --> 00:00:52,686
the variables.

27
00:00:53,552 --> 00:00:55,808
The area is x times y.

28
00:00:56,292 --> 00:00:58,497
But y changes whenever x does, so we

29
00:00:58,538 --> 00:00:59,600
can't differentiate yet.

30
00:01:00,384 --> 00:01:02,020
Use the constraint to replace y.

31
00:01:02,886 --> 00:01:04,848
y equals forty minus two x,

32
00:01:05,350 --> 00:01:08,414
so A equals x, times forty minus two

33
00:01:08,555 --> 00:01:10,958
x, which is forty x minus two x

34
00:01:10,999 --> 00:01:11,378
squared.

35
00:01:11,961 --> 00:01:13,796
Now the area depends on x alone.

36
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:16,823
Which values of x make a real pen?

37
00:01:17,890 --> 00:01:19,916
x has to be positive, or there's no

38
00:01:19,977 --> 00:01:20,217
width.

39
00:01:20,761 --> 00:01:22,488
And y has to be positive too.

40
00:01:23,232 --> 00:01:26,118
Forty minus two x is positive only when

41
00:01:26,339 --> 00:01:27,421
x is less than twenty.

42
00:01:28,063 --> 00:01:30,429
So the domain is x between zero and

43
00:01:30,510 --> 00:01:32,594
twenty, with neither end included.

44
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:35,132
At each end the pen collapses.

45
00:01:35,898 --> 00:01:37,785
Near zero it's a thin strip along the

46
00:01:37,827 --> 00:01:40,417
wall, and near twenty it's squashed flat against

47
00:01:40,458 --> 00:01:40,517
it.

48
00:01:41,321 --> 00:01:43,146
The area gets close to zero at both

49
00:01:43,247 --> 00:01:45,734
ends, but those aren't pens, so zero is

50
00:01:45,775 --> 00:01:47,820
a limit, not a value the area reaches.

51
00:01:48,905 --> 00:01:51,573
Stating the domain matters, because it decides which

52
00:01:51,675 --> 00:01:54,303
stationary points count, and what we compare at

53
00:01:54,324 --> 00:01:54,685
the ends.

54
00:01:55,503 --> 00:01:56,328
Now the calculus.

55
00:01:57,031 --> 00:01:59,620
A prime of x is forty minus four

56
00:01:59,780 --> 00:02:02,449
x, which is zero at x equals ten,

57
00:02:02,850 --> 00:02:03,693
inside the domain.

58
00:02:04,675 --> 00:02:06,699
Earlier in the course, we found a global

59
00:02:06,739 --> 00:02:08,724
maximum by comparing every candidate.

60
00:02:09,526 --> 00:02:12,300
Here the ends aren't candidates, because they aren't

61
00:02:12,441 --> 00:02:13,004
in the domain.

62
00:02:13,567 --> 00:02:15,754
So compare ten with the limits at the

63
00:02:15,856 --> 00:02:16,055
ends.

64
00:02:16,959 --> 00:02:19,164
A of ten is two hundred, bigger than

65
00:02:19,205 --> 00:02:19,445
both,

66
00:02:19,947 --> 00:02:22,252
and there's only one stationary point, so the

67
00:02:22,353 --> 00:02:24,859
area rises to two hundred and then falls.

68
00:02:25,622 --> 00:02:28,029
That makes two hundred the global maximum.

69
00:02:29,014 --> 00:02:30,159
Now answer the question.

70
00:02:30,782 --> 00:02:32,785
The pen is ten metres out from the

71
00:02:32,826 --> 00:02:35,609
wall and twenty metres along it, with an

72
00:02:35,751 --> 00:02:37,833
area of two hundred square metres.

73
00:02:38,677 --> 00:02:40,295
And here's why the square loses.

74
00:02:41,097 --> 00:02:43,701
Each metre along the wall costs one metre

75
00:02:43,741 --> 00:02:45,904
of fence, but each metre out from the

76
00:02:45,924 --> 00:02:48,307
wall costs two, because there are two of

77
00:02:48,347 --> 00:02:48,968
those sides.

78
00:02:49,629 --> 00:02:51,897
So the best pen is longer along the

79
00:02:51,938 --> 00:02:52,138
wall.

80
00:02:52,865 --> 00:02:53,898
Now a second problem.

81
00:02:54,582 --> 00:02:56,588
An open box is made from a square

82
00:02:56,628 --> 00:02:58,774
of card twenty-four centimetres wide.

83
00:02:59,515 --> 00:03:01,880
Equal squares of side x centimetres are cut

84
00:03:01,921 --> 00:03:04,085
from the corners, and the sides fold up.

85
00:03:04,647 --> 00:03:05,880
The height of the box is x.

86
00:03:07,431 --> 00:03:09,418
Each side of the base loses two squares,

87
00:03:09,759 --> 00:03:12,249
so the base is twenty-four minus two x,

88
00:03:12,731 --> 00:03:13,072
each way.

89
00:03:13,653 --> 00:03:16,661
So the volume is x, times twenty-four minus

90
00:03:16,721 --> 00:03:17,964
two x, all squared.

91
00:03:18,705 --> 00:03:20,909
For the domain, x must be positive to

92
00:03:20,969 --> 00:03:21,590
cut anything,

93
00:03:22,110 --> 00:03:24,594
and twenty-four minus two x must be positive

94
00:03:24,716 --> 00:03:27,118
to leave a base, so x is less

95
00:03:27,179 --> 00:03:27,679
than twelve.

96
00:03:28,402 --> 00:03:29,188
Expand first.

97
00:03:29,892 --> 00:03:33,083
V is four x cubed, minus ninety-six x

98
00:03:33,124 --> 00:03:35,612
squared, plus five hundred and seventy-six x.

99
00:03:36,315 --> 00:03:39,285
So V prime is twelve x squared, minus

100
00:03:39,325 --> 00:03:41,613
a hundred and ninety-two x, plus five hundred

101
00:03:41,633 --> 00:03:42,235
and seventy-six.

102
00:03:42,978 --> 00:03:45,668
Take out twelve and factorise, to get twelve,

103
00:03:45,848 --> 00:03:48,759
times x minus four, times x minus twelve.

104
00:03:49,443 --> 00:03:51,592
Twelve isn't in the domain, and it would

105
00:03:51,633 --> 00:03:53,380
leave no base, so reject it.

106
00:03:54,084 --> 00:03:57,033
At x equals four, V is four times

107
00:03:57,095 --> 00:03:59,803
sixteen squared, which is one thousand and twenty-four.

108
00:04:00,547 --> 00:04:02,937
Near both ends the volume shrinks towards zero,

109
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:04,686
so that's the greatest volume.

110
00:04:05,328 --> 00:04:07,934
Cut four-centimetre squares, and the box holds one

111
00:04:07,975 --> 00:04:09,798
thousand and twenty-four cubic centimetres.

112
00:04:10,530 --> 00:04:12,827
Here's the whole method in five short steps.

113
00:04:13,571 --> 00:04:13,932
Draw it,

114
00:04:14,435 --> 00:04:14,756
link it,

115
00:04:15,339 --> 00:04:15,660
limit it,

116
00:04:16,183 --> 00:04:16,523
solve it,

117
00:04:17,087 --> 00:04:17,367
say it.

118
00:04:18,453 --> 00:04:20,519
Draw the shape, and name the variables with

119
00:04:20,540 --> 00:04:21,081
their units.

120
00:04:21,845 --> 00:04:23,930
Link them with the constraint, and write the

121
00:04:23,971 --> 00:04:25,594
quantity in one variable.

122
00:04:26,498 --> 00:04:29,025
Limit x to the values the real object

123
00:04:29,186 --> 00:04:29,626
allows.

124
00:04:30,631 --> 00:04:33,021
Solve with calculus, and compare with the ends,

125
00:04:33,223 --> 00:04:34,690
whether they're values or limits.

126
00:04:35,534 --> 00:04:37,961
Then say the answer the question asked for,

127
00:04:38,544 --> 00:04:39,044
with units.

128
00:04:41,813 --> 00:04:42,283
Your turn.

129
00:04:43,089 --> 00:04:45,551
A rectangular garden with an area of fifty

130
00:04:45,612 --> 00:04:48,475
square metres is fenced on three sides, with

131
00:04:48,516 --> 00:04:49,596
a wall along the fourth.

132
00:04:50,358 --> 00:04:52,481
Find the dimensions that use the least fencing,

133
00:04:52,902 --> 00:04:54,284
and the least length of fencing.

134
00:04:54,951 --> 00:04:55,701
Pause here to answer.

135
00:05:06,420 --> 00:05:08,461
With x out from the wall and y

136
00:05:08,481 --> 00:05:08,822
along it,

137
00:05:09,502 --> 00:05:12,384
x y is fifty, so y is fifty

138
00:05:12,444 --> 00:05:12,904
over x,

139
00:05:13,445 --> 00:05:15,706
and the fencing is two x plus fifty

140
00:05:15,886 --> 00:05:18,027
over x, for x greater than zero.

141
00:05:18,928 --> 00:05:21,555
Its derivative, two minus fifty over x squared,

142
00:05:21,976 --> 00:05:23,961
is zero at x equals five.

143
00:05:24,564 --> 00:05:26,751
Near zero, and for very large x, the

144
00:05:26,792 --> 00:05:29,763
fencing grows without limit, so five gives the

145
00:05:29,824 --> 00:05:30,084
least.

146
00:05:30,667 --> 00:05:33,023
That's five metres by ten, with twenty metres

147
00:05:33,064 --> 00:05:33,466
of fencing.

148
00:05:34,492 --> 00:05:36,620
x equals five alone doesn't answer the question.

149
00:05:37,970 --> 00:05:38,394
Last one.

150
00:05:39,079 --> 00:05:41,303
An open box is made from a rectangle

151
00:05:41,324 --> 00:05:44,790
of card sixteen centimetres by ten centimetres, by

152
00:05:44,851 --> 00:05:47,536
cutting equal squares from the corners and folding

153
00:05:47,597 --> 00:05:48,177
up the sides.

154
00:05:49,100 --> 00:05:50,664
Find the side of the squares that gives

155
00:05:50,705 --> 00:05:53,072
the greatest volume, and state that volume.

156
00:05:53,856 --> 00:05:54,703
Pause here to answer.

157
00:06:05,327 --> 00:06:08,132
The volume is x, times sixteen minus two

158
00:06:08,273 --> 00:06:09,935
x, times ten minus two x,

159
00:06:10,537 --> 00:06:13,121
and the shorter side keeps x between zero

160
00:06:13,262 --> 00:06:13,943
and five.

161
00:06:14,646 --> 00:06:17,277
The derivative is four, times three x minus

162
00:06:17,318 --> 00:06:19,266
twenty, times x minus two.

163
00:06:20,010 --> 00:06:21,937
Twenty over three is more than five, so

164
00:06:22,078 --> 00:06:22,499
reject it.

165
00:06:23,242 --> 00:06:25,711
V of two is two times twelve times

166
00:06:25,752 --> 00:06:28,241
six, a hundred and forty-four cubic centimetres.

167
00:06:28,945 --> 00:06:31,220
Twenty over three would make the ten-centimetre side

168
00:06:31,302 --> 00:06:31,623
negative.

169
00:06:33,301 --> 00:06:36,234
So the constraint builds the function, and the

170
00:06:36,294 --> 00:06:37,801
real object sets the domain.

171
00:06:38,845 --> 00:06:40,887
Next, a different kind of model, where the

172
00:06:40,947 --> 00:06:43,329
